load @/code/algebra/cayley-dickson
  find cayley-dickson-double

load @/code/algebra/normed-division
  find normed-division-algebra

# The octonions are the Cayley-Dickson double of the quaternions, the eight-dimensional normed division algebra. They are the last rung of the tower. The input quaternions are associative, so the double keeps the norm, but the octonions are themselves the first non-associative algebra, so doubling once more, to the sedenions, loses the norm. So the octonions are the maximal reversible algebra, the upper jaw of the pinch-point.
form octonion
  link source, like cayley-dickson-double
  link algebra, like normed-division-algebra

# The pinch-point: the dimension is forced to eight, two ways at once, proof-checked by `seed test`.

# The reversibility ceiling (the upper jaw): a normed division algebra exists only up to dimension eight. The octonions
# at eight are below the next rung, the sedenions at sixteen, which exceeds eight and loses the norm. So eight is the
# last dimension that keeps it.
hold <the octonions at eight are below the sedenions at sixteen>
  call is-below
    code 8
    code 16
hold <sixteen exceeds the ceiling of eight>
  call is-above
    code 16
    code 8

# The one-substance floor (the lower jaw): the half-spinor and the vector meet at eight. Half-spinor size is
# two-to-the-(n/2 minus 1), so it is 4 at dimension six (below the vector six), two cubed at dimension eight (equal to
# the vector eight), and 16 at dimension ten (above the vector ten). The crossing happens exactly at eight.
hold <below eight the spinor is smaller than the vector>
  call is-below
    code 4
    code 6
hold <at eight the half-spinor two cubed equals the vector eight>
  call is-equal
    call multiply
      call multiply
        code 2
        code 2
      code 2
    code 8
hold <above eight the spinor is larger than the vector>
  call is-above
    code 16
    code 10

# The norm is multiplicative for EVERY pair of octonions, Degen's eight-square identity. With p and q octonions of
# integer coordinates, the squared norm of the product p q equals the product of the squared norms. This is the
# composition property at the top of the reversible tower, the maximal normed division algebra, the upper jaw of the
# pinch-point. A universal law over all sixteen coordinates, proved by the commutative-ring normalizer (the identity
# was generated by the Cayley-Dickson doubling of the quaternions, so it is correct by construction).
task octonion-norm-is-multiplicative
  take a0, like integer
  take a1, like integer
  take a2, like integer
  take a3, like integer
  take b0, like integer
